{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553971-vtm-20a-celerity-question","id":1553971,"title":"VTM 20A Celerity question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-22T19:44:27-07:00","id":1553971,"title":"VTM 20A Celerity question","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Is it me or does this contradict itself? See the bold italics. The first part says the extra actions happen at the beginning of the turn. The 2nd part says at the end of the turn. What is it?</span><br /> <br /> System: Each point of Celerity adds one die to every<br /> Dexterity-related dice roll.<i><b><u> In addition, the player can<br /> spend one blood point to take an extra action up to the<br /> number of dots he has in Celerity at the beginning of<br /> the relevant turn</u></b></i>; this expenditure can go beyond her<br /> normal Generation maximum. Any dots used for extra<br /> actions, however, are no longer available for Dexterity-related rolls during that turn. These additional actions must be physical (e.g., the vampire cannot use a<br /> mental Discipline like Dominate multiple times in one<br /> turn), <u><i><b>and extra actions occur at the end of the turn</b></i></u><br /> (the vampire\u2019s regular action still takes place per her initiative roll).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-22T20:30:21-07:00","id":1553972,"title":"","content":"You spend the blood at the beginning of your turn, and take your Celerity actions at the end of the turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T11:49:00-07:00","id":1554231,"title":"","content":"Note that your ordinary action happens on regular initiative, only the celerity actions take place at the very end of the turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25590-erafiel","name":"Erafiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25590_1.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T17:38:56-07:00","id":1554234,"title":"","content":"As was said, you spend your Celerity points at the start of your turn. Then you and everyone else takes actions as normal. Then at the end of the turn everyone who spent Blood Points to activate Celerity gets to take their Celerity actions.<br /> <br /> The design intent for this is to make sure that other players and opponents get their actions too. It prevents &quot;celerity alpha strikes&quot; where one player takes 4 or 5 actions right at the top of the round and kill everything before anyone else has a chance to take a turn. That's not a lot of fun for the other people at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}